WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.975
Crypto agility is the ability to change cryptographic algorithms, keys, libraries,

00:00:04.975 --> 00:00:07.000
and protocols without redesigning an entire system.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.948
It is not a slogan; it is an architectural property.

00:00:09.948 --> 00:00:13.000
A crypto-agile system avoids hard-coded assumptions,

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.985
keeps algorithms configurable where appropriate, supports versioned protocol negotiation,

00:00:16.985 --> 00:00:18.895
separates policy from implementation,

00:00:18.895 --> 00:00:23.000
and gives teams a realistic way to test and deploy changes without emergency rewrites.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.995
Prioritization should be risk-based.

00:00:24.995 --> 00:00:28.520
Systems protecting sensitive data with a long confidentiality lifetime deserve early

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.275
attention,

00:00:29.275 --> 00:00:32.920
especially if they are exposed to untrusted networks or depend on public-key encryption

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.000
and key establishment.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.445
Operationally critical systems also need careful planning because outages can be more

00:00:38.445 --> 00:00:40.000
damaging than delayed migration.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.980
Dependency complexity matters as well.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:46.210
A service may be ready internally but blocked by a client library, partner integration,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.190
hardware module, certificate authority, or vendor product.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.195
Hybrid approaches may appear during the transition.

00:00:52.195 --> 00:00:52.728
Conceptually,

00:00:52.728 --> 00:00:56.685
a hybrid design combines an existing mechanism with a post-quantum mechanism so the system

00:00:56.685 --> 00:01:00.000
can manage interoperability and risk while the ecosystem matures.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Hybrid does not mean automatically safer in every implementation,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.940
and it does not remove the need for testing.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:09.940
It is a migration strategy that must be evaluated in the context of protocols, libraries,

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.995
performance, failure behavior, and operational visibility.

00:01:11.995 --> 00:01:15.000
A practical plan uses pilots before broad rollout.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.940
Teams test interoperability, measure performance, review logging, validate monitoring,

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.000
confirm certificate and key lifecycle behavior, coordinate with vendors,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.940
and define fallback criteria.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:28.783
The danger is a rushed replacement that breaks systems or silently weakens security.

00:01:28.783 --> 00:01:32.000
A disciplined migration creates decision records, tracks readiness,

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.000
and moves high-risk use cases forward while keeping production stable.
